# hypernix.multilama

One interface over several llama.cpp variants (vanilla, ik_llama.cpp, PrismML fork, KoboldCpp, Nanbeige fork) for GGUF models a single backend can't all load.

## Documentation pages

- [Llama Easy](../../#/docs/Llama-Easy) · [MDXL source](pages/Llama-Easy.mdxl)

## API reference

[Open the API reference source](pages/api-reference.mdxl)

### `MultiLlamaError(code, message)`

A real, coded failure — see ``.code``. Never swallowed into a fake reply.

### `locate_binary(backend) -> Path | None`

An already-available binary for ``backend`` — env override, then

### `fetch_binary(backend, quiet=False, search_releases=10) -> Path`

Download+cache a prebuilt server binary for ``backend``.

### `ensure_binary(backend, quiet=False) -> Path`

locate_binary(), falling back to fetch_binary() if nothing's found.

### `shutdown_all_servers() -> None`

Terminate every server subprocess this module has launched.

### `MultiLlama(backend, repo_id, filename, gguf_path, n_gpu_layers, n_ctx, _python_llm=None)`

A loaded GGUF model, backed by whichever llama.cpp variant answered

### `MultiLlama.chat_message(messages, system=None, max_tokens=512, temperature=0.7, tools=None) -> dict[str, Any]`

Like :meth:`chat`, but returns the raw OpenAI-style message dict

### `load(repo_id, filename, backend='vanilla', n_gpu_layers=-1, n_ctx=8192, quiet=False) -> MultiLlama`

Load a GGUF model through ``backend`` (see :data:`BACKENDS`).

### `auto_select_backend(repo_id, filename) -> str`

Best-effort default backend for a given GGUF, based on naming

### `status_json() -> dict[str, Any]`

Serializable availability report for every registered backend —

